{"abstract":"Understanding how phytoplankton interacts with local and regional drivers as well as their feedbacks is a great challenge, and quantitative analyses of the regulating role of human activities and climate changes on these feedback loops are also limited. By using monthly monitoring dataset (2000–2017) from Lake Taihu and empirical dynamic modelling to construct causal networks, we quantified the strengths of causal feedbacks among phytoplankton, local environments, zooplankton, meteorology as well as global climate oscillation. Prevalent bidirectional causal linkages between phytoplankton biomass (chlorophyll a) and the tested drivers were found, providing holistic and quantitative evidence of the ubiquitous feedback loops. Phytoplankton biomass exhibited the highest feedbacks with total inorganic nitrogen and ammonia and the lowest with nitrate. The feedbacks between phytoplankton biomass and environmental factors from 2000 to 2017 could be classified into two groups: the local environments (e.g., nutrients, pH, transparency, zooplankton biomass)-driven enhancement loops promoting the response of the phytoplankton biomass, and the climate (e.g., wind speed)-driven regulatory loops suppressing it. The two counterbalanced groups modified the emergent macroecological patterns. Our findings revealed that the causal feedback networks loosened significantly after 2007 following nutrient loading reduction and unsuccessful biomanipulation restoration attempts by stocking carp. The strength of enhancement loops underwent marked decreases leading to reduced phytoplankton responses to the tested drivers, while the climate (decreasing wind speed, warming winter)-driven regulatory loops increased– like a tug-of-war. To counteract the self-amplifying feedback loops, the present eutrophication mitigation efforts, especially nutrient reduction, should be continued, and introduction of alternative measures to indirectly regulate the critical components (e.g., pH, Secchi depth, zooplankton biomass) of the loops would be beneficial.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Fu, Hui","Ge, Yili","Cai, Guojun","Deng, Jianmin","Liu, Huanyao","Wu, Aiping","Li, Youzhi","Li, Wei","Yuan, Guixiang","Jeppesen, Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-728108"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Fu, Hui"],"country":["China","Turkey"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CAS - Nanjing Institute of Geography and Limnology","Hunan Agricultural University","Middle East Technical University","Nanchang Institute of Technology","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","Yunnan University"],"keyword":["Causal linkages","Convergent Cross Mapping","Eutrophication","Feedback loops","Lake ecosystem"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"weakened casual feedback loops following intensive restoration efforts and climate changes in a large shallow freshwater lake","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85181586732","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-728108","identifier":[{"id":"38159751","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85181586732","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-a67754d6-33e1-41de-9e1b-46b242b9b269"],"keyword":["Causal linkages","Convergent cross mapping","Eutrophication","Feedback loops","Lake ecosystem"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BA14BF4B0FB5F9383118B8D6A394DFFC"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"hunan agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Hunan Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"cas nanjing institute of geography and limnology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"CAS - Nanjing Institute of Geography and Limnology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"nanchang institute of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Nanchang Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Freshwater Ecology","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, WATEC, Centre for Water Technology, WATEC, Centre for Water Technology - WATEC Aarhus University Centre for Water Technology, C.F. Møllers Allé 3"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"university of chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"tr","key":"middle east technical university","loc":["Turkey","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Middle East Technical University","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"cn","key":"yunnan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Yunnan University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hui","key":"fuhuipau","last":"Fu","name":"Fu, Hui","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yili","key":"geyilipau","last":"Ge","name":"Ge, Yili","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Guojun","key":"caiguojunpau","last":"Cai","name":"Cai, Guojun","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jianmin","key":"dengjianminpau","last":"Deng","name":"Deng, Jianmin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Huanyao","key":"liuhuanyaopau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Huanyao","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aiping","key":"wuaipingpau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Aiping","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Youzhi","key":"liyouzhipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Youzhi","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"liweipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Wei","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Guixiang","key":"yuanguixiangpau","last":"Yuan","name":"Yuan, Guixiang","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5 6 7","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik","key":"jeppesenerikpau","last":"Jeppesen","locid":"22bb5d6e-a9ae-4f70-81da-df1c57e71163","name":"Jeppesen, Erik","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38159751"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.scitotenv.2023.169601","issn":["00489697","18791026"],"issn_org":["00489697"],"journal":"Science of the Total Environment","paperid":"169601","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Science of the Total Environment","volume":"913"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85181586732"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a67754d6-33e1-41de-9e1b-46b242b9b269"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Weakened casual feedback loops following intensive restoration efforts and climate changes in a large shallow freshwater lake","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-728108","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Phytoplankton communities are crucial components of aquatic ecosystems, and since they are highly interactive, they always form complex networks. Yet, our understanding of how interactive phytoplankton networks vary through time under changing environmental conditions is limited. Using a 29-year (339 months) long-term dataset on Lake Taihu, China, we constructed a temporal network comprising monthly sub-networks using “extended Local Similarity Analysis” and assessed how eutrophication, climate change, and restoration efforts influenced the temporal dynamics of network complexity and stability. The network architecture of phytoplankton showed strong dynamic changes with varying environments. Our results revealed cascading effects of eutrophication and climate change on phytoplankton network stability via changes in network complexity. The network stability of phytoplankton increased with average degree, modularity, and nestedness and decreased with connectance. Eutrophication (increasing nitrogen) stabilized the phytoplankton network, mainly by increasing its average degree, while climate change, i.e., warming and decreasing wind speed enhanced its stability by increasing the cohesion of phytoplankton communities directly and by decreasing the connectance of network indirectly. A remarkable shift and a major decrease in the temporal dynamics of phytoplankton network complexity (average degree, nestedness) and stability (robustness, persistence) were detected after 2007 when numerous eutrophication mitigation efforts (not all successful) were implemented, leading to simplified phytoplankton networks and reduced stability. Our findings provide new insights into the organization of phytoplankton networks under eutrophication (or re-oligotrophication) and climate change in subtropical shallow lakes.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Cai, Guojun","Ge, Yili","Dong, Zheng","Liao, Yu","Chen, Yaoqi","Wu, Aiping","Li, Youzhi","Liu, Huanyao","Yuan, Guixiang","Deng, Jianming","Fu, Hui","Jeppesen, Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-745332"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Deng, Jianming","Fu, Hui"],"country":["China","Turkey"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CAS - Nanjing Institute of Geography and Limnology","Guizhou Institute of Technology","Hunan Agricultural University","Middle East Technical University","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","Yunnan University"],"keyword":["Climate change","Complex systems","Ecosystem dynamics","Ecosystem stability","Eutrophication","Species interactions","Temporal network"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"temporal shifts in the phytoplankton network in a large eutrophic shallow freshwater lake subjected to major environmental changes due to human interventions","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85197754771","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-745332","identifier":[{"id":"38986279","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85197754771","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c8f70124-ab64-4604-a612-b72dd2e633fd"],"keyword":["Climate change","Complex systems","Ecosystem dynamics","Ecosystem stability","Eutrophication","Species interactions","Temporal network"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-55D3D6810412462D0E83BDD24A68A0E2"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"hunan agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Hunan Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"guizhou institute of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Guizhou Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"cas nanjing institute of geography and limnology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"CAS - Nanjing Institute of Geography and Limnology","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Freshwater Ecology","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, WATEC, Centre for Water Technology, WATEC, Centre for Water Technology - WATEC Aarhus University Centre for Water Technology, C.F. Møllers Allé 3"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"university of chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"tr","key":"middle east technical university","loc":["Turkey","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Middle East Technical University","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"cn","key":"yunnan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Yunnan University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Guojun","key":"caipau","last":"Cai","name":"Cai, Guojun","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yili","key":"gepau","last":"Ge","name":"Ge, Yili","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zheng","key":"dongpau","last":"Dong","name":"Dong, Zheng","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yu","key":"liaopau","last":"Liao","name":"Liao, Yu","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yaoqi","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Yaoqi","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aiping","key":"wupau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Aiping","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Youzhi","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Youzhi","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Huanyao","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Huanyao","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Guixiang","key":"yuanpau","last":"Yuan","name":"Yuan, Guixiang","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jianming","key":"dengpau","last":"Deng","name":"Deng, Jianming","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hui","key":"fupau","last":"Fu","name":"Fu, Hui","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5 6 7","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik","key":"jeppesenpau","last":"Jeppesen","locid":"22bb5d6e-a9ae-4f70-81da-df1c57e71163","name":"Jeppesen, Erik","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38986279"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.watres.2024.122054","issn":["00431354","18792448"],"issn_org":["00431354"],"journal":"Water Research","paperid":"122054","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Water Research","volume":"261"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85197754771"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c8f70124-ab64-4604-a612-b72dd2e633fd"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Temporal shifts in the phytoplankton network in a large eutrophic shallow freshwater lake subjected to major environmental changes due to human interventions","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-745332","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The aquatic environment in lake ecosystems is greatly affected by human activities and global climate change, while studies on the cascading effects on water environments using a holistic approach are scarce. We employed generalized least squares (GLS) modeling to assess the annual trends in water quality of Lake Poyang from 1983 to 2018 and found that total nitrogen (TN), ammonia nitrogen (NH4), and the chemical oxygen demand (CODMn) increased, while total phosphorus (TP) showed no significant changes. Moreover, Cross-correlation function analyses demonstrated that following the Three Gorges Dam (TGD) operation, the influence of human activities, such as grain yield per unit area (GYP) and urban population (Upop), on water quality became more pronounced, while the role of regional meteorological factors like the monthly maximum value of daily minimum temperature (TNX) decreased. Generalized multilevel path models (GMPMs) revealed that human activities (GPY, Upop, fertilizer application) as well as climate (El Niño-Southern Oscillation (ENSO), meteorology) affected the water quality variables directly or indirectly via the hydrology (sediment discharge, water level). Thus, hydrology dominated the changes in TP (31.6 %) and TN (25.2 %), while human activities controlled the changes in NH4 (17.9 %) to a higher extent and meteorology the changes in CODMn (21.3 %). By contrast, ENSO exerted a relatively weak control on the water quality variables. Our results highlighted that regional meteorology as well as hydrology strongly modified the cascading effects of ENSO and human activities on water quality.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Ge, Yili","Wu, Zhouhang","Chen, Yaoqi","Guo, Peiqin","Wu, Aiping","Liu, Huanyao","Yuan, Guixiang","Li, Youzhi","Fu, Hui","Jeppesen, Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-762911"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Li, Youzhi"],"country":["China","Turkey"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hunan Agricultural University","Middle East Technical University","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"keyword":["El Niño Southern Oscillation","Eutrophication","Human Activities","Hydrology","Meteorology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cascading effects of human activities and enso on the water quality of poyang lake in china","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85203816302","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-762911","identifier":[{"id":"85203816302","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-36ad35cc-ea9d-41c0-b689-0a5d29f5b8db"],"keyword":["El Niño‐Southern Oscillation","Eutrophication","Human activities","Hydrology","Meteorology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FBC9BED3EB205FCE257AFAA884730B78"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"hunan agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Hunan Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Freshwater Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"university of chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"tr","key":"middle east technical university","loc":["Turkey","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Middle East Technical University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yili","key":"geyilipau","last":"Ge","name":"Ge, Yili","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhouhang","key":"wuzhouhangpau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Zhouhang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yaoqi","key":"chenyaoqipau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Yaoqi","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peiqin","key":"guopeiqinpau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Peiqin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aiping","key":"wuaipingpau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Aiping","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Huanyao","key":"liuhuanyaopau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Huanyao","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Guixiang","key":"yuanguixiangpau","last":"Yuan","name":"Yuan, Guixiang","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Youzhi","key":"liyouzhipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Youzhi","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hui","key":"fuhuipau","last":"Fu","name":"Fu, Hui","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik","key":"jeppesenerikpau","last":"Jeppesen","locid":"22bb5d6e-a9ae-4f70-81da-df1c57e71163","name":"Jeppesen, Erik","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.catena.2024.108380","issn":["03418162","18726887"],"issn_org":["03418162"],"journal":"Catena","paperid":"108380","publisher":"Catena Verlag GmbH","status":"p","title":"Catena","volume":"246"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85203816302"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-36ad35cc-ea9d-41c0-b689-0a5d29f5b8db"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Cascading effects of human activities and ENSO on the water quality of Poyang Lake in China","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-762911","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Human activities and climate change are two major stressors affecting lake ecosystems as well as phytoplankton communities worldwide. However, how the temporal dynamics of phytoplankton are directly or indirectly linked to anthropogenic activities and climatic oscillation remains unclear. We assessed the annual trends (1988–2018) in phytoplankton abundance (PA) in Lake Dongting, China and related it to five groups of variables characterizing human activities, global climate oscillation, water nutrients, hydrology, and meteorology. We found a significant increase in PA, urbanization (Upop), total nitrogen (TN), fertilizer application (FA), number of summer days (SU), and the warm speed duration index (WSDI) and a significant decrease in the water discharge of three inlets (TIWD) and the sediment discharge of three inlets (TISD) and four tributaries (FTSD) and the net sediment deposition (NSD). However, no significant annual trends were observed for the number of rainstorm days (R50mm), the simple precipitation intensity index (SDII) and yearly anomalies of El Niño-Southern oscillation events (ENSOi). Cross-correlation Function analyses demonstrated that the operation of the Three George Dam (TGD) strengthened the effects of hydrology, rainfall patterns and ENSOi on phytoplankton, but strongly weakened the association between water nutrients, human activities and phytoplankton abundance. Path analysis revealed that TP, TN, FA, R50 mm as well as WSDI had a direct positive effect on PA, while a direct negative effect was found for ENSO i, NSD and TISD. Human activities (Upop and FA), warming (WSDI and SU), and rainfall patterns (SDII and R50 mm) exerted indirect controls on phytoplankton through changes in water nutrients and hydrology. Climate change (ENSOi) had a direct effect on PA, but also showed twelve indirect pathways via changes in hydrology and meteorology (both positive and negative effects were found). Overall, meteorology contributed most markedly to the variations of PA (29.3%), followed by hydrology (25.3%), human activities (24%), water nutrients (10.5%), and ENSOi (1.9%). Our results highlight a strongly causal connection between human activities as well as global climate change and phytoplankton and the benefits of considering multiple environmental drivers in determining the temporal dynamics of lake biotic communities.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Fu, Hui","Chen, Lidan","Ge, Yili","Wu, Alping","Liu, Hyanyao","Li, Wei","Yuan, Guixiang","Jeppesen, Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-154306"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Fu, Hui","Yuan, Guixiang"],"country":["China","Turkey"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hunan Agricultural University","Middle East Technical University","Nanchang Institute of Technology","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"keyword":["El Niño Southern Oscillation","Eutrophication","Hydrology","Meteorology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"linking human activities and global climatic oscillation to phytoplankton dynamics in a subtropical lake","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85119209561","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-154306","identifier":[{"id":"34800853","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85119209561","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-2ba51208-456b-4855-bba0-bef97e111b25"],"keyword":["El Niño‐Southern oscillation","Eutrophication","Hydrology","Meteorology","Water nutrients"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-678B83A90659D3E563D8307834E7BA46"],"oai":{"class":"Bloc